ying to make a book so I didn't  have access to any of that stuff  but what I did was I just did tons of  Google searches yeah and usually what  happens is that when an author hits a  million copies or four million or  whatever yeah yeah they'll let you know  yeah they let you know and so there's  all kinds of stuff or you'll find like  if you just search a title and then copy  sold  there's New York Times articles that  profile an author and they say you know  that book sold six million copies or  whatever so it was just a bunch of leg  work like that  anyway I put together that spreadsheet  let's say I got like 150 titles or  something and then I started to look for  patterns so what format do all these  titles follow and I think I ended up  coming up with they're about six I won't  be able to remember them all off the top  of my head but the most common format is  the blank of blank so the Power of Habit  the life-changing magic of tidying up  The Power of Now the power of positive  thinking  the subtle art of not giving a [ __ ] the  blah blah so it's always the blank of  blank and that's a very proven the war  of art it's a very proven format and the  psychology of money like we just keep  going on and on and on there's so many  examples like that and usually what  people do is they take their topic and  that's the second piece and then they  take some type of descriptor and that's  the first one and ideally you're  combining things that are not usually  combined so  like the life-changing magic of tidying  up so tidying up is the topic of the  book but now you're telling me that it's  life-changing and what you find is a lot  of these best-selling books they have  some element of contrast in the title  there's something that's unexpected  about it so even the another common  format is you just take and this is of  not giving a [ __ ] right you don't  usually exactly like yeah the f word is  actually the least subtle thing right so  like there's this interestin